      "title": "ℹ️ Popup Preview",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# NKD Popup Prewiew\n\nThis is one of my babies.\n\nAt its core, it’s just an image preview node, but it comes with a few quality-of-life perks.\n\n### Open viewer\n\nThe coolest part is that once you’ve rendered a preview, you can pop it out into a floating window. You can drag it anywhere on your screen or even move it to a second monitor, which is super handy for inpainting since you don’t have to keep jumping back to the image node.\n\n### Copy Image\n\nIt’s just a simple button to copy the image so you don't have to deal with opening menus. This is super handy if you're jumping between Comfy and software like Krita or Photoshop, or any other program where you need to copy images to work with layers.\n\n### Primary mode\n\nIf you hit the \"set as primary\" button, you’ll see a blue border appear around the node. This sets it to work with customizable hotkeys in the config settings.\n\n- **Q** = Open the viewer. you can use them to pull up the viewer wirelessly whenever you need it. <br>\n- **Shift + Q** = Calculate this preview only. These one let you render the \"primary\" viewer without triggering the rest of the workflow.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#223",
      "bgcolor": "#335"
    },
    {
      "id": 1368,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
